ughly $1.7 million and holds about $1 million on hand, while Vincent has raised under $300,000, leaving a large financial gap heading into the final stretch.\n\nThe only recent poll, sponsored by a Democratic firm in late July, showed Fry ahead by four points, but its sample and sponsorship warrant caution. Prediction markets give Fry about a 95 percent chance of winning. Fry's simultaneous run for the Senate seat adds a wrinkle, but his name recognition, incumbency, and the district's lean make him the clear favorite, with Vincent needing an unexpected shift to compete.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0379, "margin": -13.69}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0396, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0447, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0469, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0326, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.036, "margin": -14.0}]}